  "summary_en": "Ecuador's civil aviation authority resolution approving RDAC 101, a binding regulation on unmanned aircraft systems up to 250 kg. It sets open, specific and certified operating categories, registration, remote pilot authorisation, operator certificates, risk assessment, insurance and liability, BVLOS and autonomous operation limits, and no-fly zones, replacing the 2024 RPAS rules.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Three operational categories (open ≤4 kg, specific ≤250 kg, certified reserved) with differing requirements.",
   "Mandatory UAS registration for aircraft over 250 g and remote pilot authorisation for specific category.",
   "UAS Operation Certificate (UOC), operational risk assessment and SMS required for commercial/private specific operations.",
   "Autonomous operation allowed only with ability to take control, limited to 1,000 m unless UOC or special authorisation.",
   "Third-party liability insurance with minimum coverage by MTOW; operator directly liable; accident reporting within 24 hours."
  ],
